issue.description:
Child 2 of 5, SEVENTH split round for umbrella pdfphp-24ad380b. Depends on child pdfphp-012e82d4 (forwarded-fields contract verdict). Scope: the negative teeth of the field-minimality pin ONLY - tests/ClientBufferedRouteTest.php::test_extract_forwards_options_as_the_only_snake_case_fields (line 331).

For each leak class below, temporarily break src/Client.php so exactly that leak ships, run the pin, and record the observed failure (assertion message, line, and the true exit code captured without a pipe), then revert with git checkout and confirm `git status --porcelain -- src tests` is empty before the next class:
(a) an unexpected extra field rides along;
(b) a camelCase name replaces a snake_case one;
(c) an explicit false or null is resurrected (no_cache=false is the load-bearing case - the serve API reads presence as true);
(d) the client-side timeout option is forwarded;
(e) a forwarded value is mangled in transit.
Every class must be observed to fire the pin (exit 1). A class that survives is under-specification: tighten the test to catch it, commit and push to Forgejo origin (plain push only, never force-push), and re-prove the tightened pin with the same mutation. Do not touch the file-Source pin (child 4 owns it) or the interaction test.

Acceptance:
- Five recorded mutation observations (class, mutation, failure message, exit code) plus a revert check after each.
- vendor/bin/phpunit tests/ClientBufferedRouteTest.php exits 0 on PHP 8.2 after all reverts (baseline: OK, 44 tests, 222 assertions).
- Any fix committed and pushed; no coverage from other slices deleted or weakened; tests/Retired excluded and inert.

Environment note (repeat in every shell): PHP and composer are NOT on PATH on this box. Export `export PATH=/nix/store/22x54ar7f5sv6qpzbs635hbm9425gw83-php-with-extensions-8.2.28/bin:/nix/store/bfbww3vdbqmaz8p1jrknkxsjvv3zkv1h-composer-2.8.5/bin:$PATH` before any phpunit/composer call - vendor/bin/phpunit has a `#!/usr/bin/env php` shebang, so without it it exits 127 with NO output, which has been mistaken for a pass. Empty phpunit output = missing binary, not success.
